WEBVTT

00:01.710 --> 00:04.000
<i>Rick's return
didn't save the Earth team.</i>

00:05.920 --> 00:07.760
<i>His injuries
from the crash in the first race</i>

00:07.930 --> 00:09.930
<i>were much worse than we thought.</i>

00:11.550 --> 00:14.600
<i>Rick Thunderbolt,
champion star-racer pilot,</i>

00:14.770 --> 00:16.140
<i>will never fly again.</i>

00:16.850 --> 00:19.190
<i>Young Molly is back
in the driver's</i> seat.

00:20.900 --> 00:21.900
<i>The good news is...</i>

00:22.190 --> 00:23.900
<i>She's won her fourth race.</i>

00:24.360 --> 00:25.610
<i>The bad news is...</i>

00:25.780 --> 00:27.780
<i>With all the extra work
she's giving us,</i>

00:27.950 --> 00:30.240
<i>we'll never see
the light of day again.</i>

02:21.430 --> 02:22.890
Good morning, my friend.

02:23.060 --> 02:25.270
You're not
at the preselection ceremony?

02:25.440 --> 02:27.860
Racing has lost its appeal
for me lately.

02:28.190 --> 02:29.480
What can I offer you?

02:29.650 --> 02:31.780
<i>lard carries on“;
the very best...</i>

02:31.940 --> 02:34.070
machinery, imports, local goods.

02:34.240 --> 02:36.110
Zard's got everything you need.

02:36.410 --> 02:38.450
Take a look at this part.

02:39.200 --> 02:41.580
It came off my former star-racer.

02:41.870 --> 02:44.540
Sorry, my friend.
Spare parts are not Zard's thing.

02:44.920 --> 02:48.380
An explosion did this to my ship.
Some local explosives.

02:48.500 --> 02:50.750
Your pals in the souk sent me here.

02:51.050 --> 02:52.840
They told me explosives
are Zard's thing

02:53.050 --> 02:54.470
because you make them.

02:58.890 --> 03:00.100
Come back here, Scrub!

03:08.610 --> 03:11.270
The six remaining pilots
please step forward.

03:12.230 --> 03:15.070
Here's our big moment.
Shake a leg, Molly.

03:19.030 --> 03:19.780
Pilots only.

03:20.200 --> 03:21.790
Please return to your seat.

03:22.040 --> 03:25.540
Guess I'll be watching
with Don Wei, real thrilling.

03:26.000 --> 03:27.000
Go on. It's OK.

03:32.420 --> 03:34.340
Why do pilots have all the fun?

03:50.730 --> 03:53.860
<i>96 teams were called to Alwas,</i>

03:54.230 --> 03:57.110
<i>and now only 6 remain.</i>

03:57.950 --> 04:00.780
<i>It's a miracle
we've made it this far.</i>

04:35.400 --> 04:36.530
The Avatar.

04:36.940 --> 04:40.280
Well, we're certainly not
in Kansas anymore.

04:46.790 --> 04:50.500
Congratulations, proud pilots.

04:51.960 --> 04:55.750
Toros, Colonel
of the Crog lmperium.

04:56.710 --> 05:00.010
Rush, from Planet Byrus.

05:04.220 --> 05:10.100
The special envoy
of Planet Adalou, Super-Racer.

05:13.560 --> 05:14.690
Nice outfit.

05:14.860 --> 05:18.690
Aikka, prince of Nourasia.

05:20.490 --> 05:22.110
Prince Aikka.

05:27.410 --> 05:32.080
The representative
of the Earth Coalition, Molly.

05:34.460 --> 05:39.340
And Spirit,
Ambassador of the Phils.

05:52.480 --> 05:54.900
<i>That... that face...</i>

05:58.190 --> 06:00.690
<i>No, it cannot be him.</i>

06:02.740 --> 06:07.370
Now, you shall all race
in turns against each other.

06:07.530 --> 06:11.000
Each victory will earn
the winner one point.

06:11.200 --> 06:13.670
At the end of six races,

06:13.830 --> 06:16.920
the three pilots
with the highest score

06:17.090 --> 06:18.710
shall be deemed worthy

06:18.880 --> 06:23.170
to go to the Grand Finals
on the Planet Oban.

06:26.260 --> 06:28.350
<i>I think I can do it, Dad.</i>

06:28.850 --> 06:31.390
<i>But I need you
to believe in me down there.</i>

06:34.900 --> 06:37.940
Race like the wind, champions,

06:38.110 --> 06:39.650
towards Oban

06:39.820 --> 06:43.320
and towards the Ultimate Prize.

06:53.500 --> 06:56.630
Why did I accept that deal?
I knew that there would be trouble.

07:02.050 --> 07:05.380
I think now is a good time
to ease your conscience, Scrub.

07:05.720 --> 07:06.340
Tell me.

07:06.970 --> 07:08.430
Don't hurt me, please.

07:09.010 --> 07:10.390
I'll tell you everything.

07:10.930 --> 07:12.430
I know who did this.

07:13.770 --> 07:15.730
Who did it?
Was it the Crogs?

07:15.890 --> 07:17.560
Are they planning
another attack?

07:17.900 --> 07:20.400
How much did you sell them?
Tell me now.

07:20.900 --> 07:22.980
I'll tell you.
I can even lead you there.

07:23.150 --> 07:25.570
But please, don't hurt me.
Please don't. Please.

07:26.450 --> 07:27.860
Then start walking.

08:06.110 --> 08:12.030
The winner of the first race
of the final playoffs is Spirit.

08:28.680 --> 08:29.550
Prince Aikka.

08:31.850 --> 08:34.180
Looks like your boyfriend
took a beating.

08:34.430 --> 08:36.180
Not that he didn't deserve it.

08:36.850 --> 08:38.600
Don't go there, Jordan.

08:39.850 --> 08:41.350
We still have to do
better than the prince.

08:41.900 --> 08:43.900
That shouldn't be too hard to do.

08:44.020 --> 08:45.480
The guy rides a bug.

08:48.490 --> 08:51.950
This prince is a grade A loser.
Why does she care so much about him?

09:04.420 --> 09:07.090
And now it's the Earth team.

09:07.260 --> 09:09.880
Challenged by Colonel Toros.

09:19.230 --> 09:21.140
Molly, look.
It's a Crog trident.

09:21.640 --> 09:24.190
That's what they used
when they attacked the Earth.

09:24.690 --> 09:25.940
I remember.

09:26.110 --> 09:28.780
They showed us the picture
at the boarding school.

09:29.070 --> 09:30.070
Listen up.

09:30.820 --> 09:33.910
Both of you. We're entering
these playoffs with a clean slate.

09:34.280 --> 09:35.740
I know Toros is tough.

09:35.910 --> 09:39.040
But that doesn't mean
we can't pull off a surprise victory.

09:40.870 --> 09:43.750
You've both shown
your ability to beat the odds.

09:44.040 --> 09:45.420
We won't let you down, sir.

09:46.710 --> 09:48.880
I heard Toros
has never been beaten.

09:49.340 --> 09:51.260
Do you seriously believe
they have a chance?

09:54.970 --> 09:57.930
If I don't believe in them,
no one will.

10:14.780 --> 10:18.450
<i>With Rick gone,
we must make do.</i>

10:26.040 --> 10:28.210
Try the other pedal, Molly.
He's gaining on us.

10:28.420 --> 10:30.590
Jordan, would you like to drive?

10:30.800 --> 10:32.170
Come on, faster.

10:42.140 --> 10:44.270
His cruising speed is
much greater than yours.

10:44.480 --> 10:46.270
You'll have to catch him
on the curves.

10:46.730 --> 10:47.610
Yes!

10:54.200 --> 10:55.610
<i>Get it together, Molly.</i>

10:55.780 --> 10:57.450
<i>You can't let Don Wei down.</i>

11:01.910 --> 11:03.040
All systems are normal.

11:03.200 --> 11:04.910
She's doing
surprisingly well, sir.

11:05.080 --> 11:06.080
It's early, Koji.

11:13.300 --> 11:14.670
This is a Crog, Molly.

11:14.970 --> 11:17.640
Stay alert, and keep clear
of the trident's blades.

11:25.140 --> 11:27.310
Oh-ho... Jordan, hang on,
we're going for a roll!

11:27.690 --> 11:28.480
Roll it!

11:36.280 --> 11:37.610
Well done, partner.

11:38.070 --> 11:41.120
Well done yourself, partner.
Keep your eyes open back there.

11:44.580 --> 11:45.250
He's back.

11:52.460 --> 11:55.220
I've got a bad feeling
about this trident.

11:56.930 --> 11:58.090
He's coming right at us!

11:59.760 --> 12:01.180
It's too early
to overtake him, Molly.

12:01.550 --> 12:03.850
Let him pass for now,
or he'll ram the Arrow 2.

12:04.020 --> 12:04.720
I'll try, sir.

12:13.190 --> 12:15.440
It's not working.
I can't shake him!

12:18.910 --> 12:19.700
<i>Or maybe...</i>

12:20.990 --> 12:22.950
<i>I can put
some distance between us.</i>

12:24.700 --> 12:25.660
Molly, what are you doing?

12:26.910 --> 12:28.370
She's engaged the hyperdrive.

12:37.130 --> 12:39.090
This girl will be the death of me.

12:41.840 --> 12:43.810
Molly, you're
out of the range of his blade.

12:43.970 --> 12:44.970
Disengage now.

12:51.100 --> 12:52.270
Molly, watch out!

12:52.610 --> 12:53.980
I can't disengage.

12:55.530 --> 12:56.320
It's too soon.

13:06.290 --> 13:08.330
Hey, I'm in heaven?

13:14.460 --> 13:15.880
What's their fuel like?

13:16.500 --> 13:17.590
Low but not critical.

13:17.760 --> 13:19.300
They're OK
for a few more seconds.

13:19.420 --> 13:21.800
They're safe from the Crog.
He's way behind.

13:27.430 --> 13:29.350
Hyperdrive disengaged, sir.

13:35.480 --> 13:38.780
Well, well, well, I must say
that I wasn't expecting you to...

13:38.940 --> 13:40.070
fare so well.

13:40.530 --> 13:43.610
Did you hear that, Jordan?
A compliment from Don Wei.

13:43.780 --> 13:44.990
We lived to hear it.

13:45.990 --> 13:48.330
Keep up your present pace
and watch your tank levels.

13:48.490 --> 13:50.160
The race is far from over.

13:54.330 --> 13:56.420
I'd love to see the look
on that Crog's face.

13:58.380 --> 14:01.090
Are you finished
playing, humans?

14:02.300 --> 14:04.470
It's been amusing
watching you struggle

14:04.640 --> 14:06.010
with your pathetic ship.

14:06.890 --> 14:08.890
But now I'm bored.

14:09.180 --> 14:10.850
Well, don't let us keep you.

14:11.350 --> 14:12.100
Farewell.

14:24.160 --> 14:24.950
What?

14:26.820 --> 14:27.620
That's not...

14:59.020 --> 15:02.190
No one can resist
the strength of the Crogs.

15:02.940 --> 15:06.360
Earth and the rest
of the Galaxy must learn.

15:06.950 --> 15:09.990
Once I have claimed
the Ultimate Prize,

15:10.790 --> 15:13.540
all shall kneel.

15:15.460 --> 15:17.380
Molly, Jordan, can you hear me?

15:18.210 --> 15:20.250
Molly, Jordan, do you copy?

15:37.480 --> 15:40.400
<i>You tricked us, Toms'.
You, you Grog'!</i>

15:40.570 --> 15:42.570
We'll have our revenge.
You'll see!

15:42.780 --> 15:44.690
You'll pay for this!

16:01.670 --> 16:02.880
Can it be fixed?

16:03.050 --> 16:06.340
Well, now we have two ships
for the price of one.

16:08.550 --> 16:09.720
One thing's certain,

16:09.890 --> 16:12.010
you can kiss
the hyperdrive goodbye.

16:13.140 --> 16:14.850
It's totally shot.

16:15.890 --> 16:19.730
Vehicles can always be repaired.
It's them I'm worried about.

16:25.030 --> 16:27.780
I've worried about them
since the beginning.

16:30.070 --> 16:33.580
They were showing
signs of progress, but now...

16:33.780 --> 16:36.200
they've clearly reached their limit.

16:39.080 --> 16:41.250
If only we'd known
more about the trident,

16:41.420 --> 16:42.790
we could have stopped him.

16:42.960 --> 16:44.170
You did your best.

16:46.880 --> 16:49.010
Our best wasn't
good enough, was it?

16:49.220 --> 16:52.640
Every champion must experience
the agony of defeat

16:52.800 --> 16:55.350
at least once
in their professional career.

16:55.520 --> 16:58.140
Toros was just too powerful.

16:58.890 --> 16:59.890
End of story.

17:00.440 --> 17:01.900
Well, that was
a nice thing to say.

17:02.060 --> 17:04.110
He didn't mean a word of it.

17:05.940 --> 17:07.570
As usual.

17:20.500 --> 17:22.630
Great stunt
you pulled out there.

17:23.830 --> 17:25.920
Want to sit down
and talk about it?

17:26.300 --> 17:27.510
What do you think?

18:02.500 --> 18:04.960
I didn't know
the Nourasian pit was so close.

18:09.380 --> 18:12.680
Easy, no one's going
to hurt you, big fella.

18:15.850 --> 18:17.810
You had a rotten day too, huh?

18:34.320 --> 18:35.780
Prince, keep your guard up.

18:35.990 --> 18:37.950
No wonder Spirit surprised you.

18:48.290 --> 18:50.550
Molly?
What are you doing here?

18:50.880 --> 18:52.470
This is not the moment.

18:52.880 --> 18:56.470
I thought you might like to talk
since we both lost the race.

18:57.050 --> 18:58.640
This is clearly a lie.

18:59.180 --> 19:01.430
Any opponent would rejoice
at our defeat.

19:01.600 --> 19:02.680
She is a spy,

19:03.140 --> 19:05.730
and we shall deal with her
as one deals with spies.

19:05.900 --> 19:08.560
Look at me.
Do I look like a spy to you?

19:11.110 --> 19:12.320
I'll handle this.

19:15.660 --> 19:16.610
Molly, wait!

19:31.340 --> 19:35.130
Why did you save me from Grooor
only to deal with me now?

19:35.720 --> 19:37.260
Deal with you?

19:37.640 --> 19:39.510
Oh, you mean this?

19:39.760 --> 19:41.220
This is for practice.

19:43.520 --> 19:45.350
I apologize for the rough reception.

19:53.280 --> 19:56.030
Nourasians are well known
for their hospitality.

20:00.070 --> 20:00.830
Come.

20:09.330 --> 20:11.840
It has been an unfortunate day.

20:12.210 --> 20:14.550
Yes. For both of us.

20:25.100 --> 20:26.350
Prince Aikka?

20:26.560 --> 20:27.850
Prince Aikka!

20:28.060 --> 20:29.730
I must be getting back.

20:30.020 --> 20:33.230
My fencing master
is a bit of a nuisance.

20:33.400 --> 20:35.360
-But he means well.
-I know the feeling.

20:35.900 --> 20:37.780
Put today's race behind you.

20:38.150 --> 20:40.070
We'll do better tomorrow.

21:21.160 --> 21:24.240
No, Master. No, please.
I said nothing!

21:24.700 --> 21:26.450
I promise you.

21:27.910 --> 21:31.040
No...
